Text cleaners
=============

A 'cleaner' turns bytes into text, one byte at a time.
A 'cleaner maker' makes a fresh cleaner from a 'starting text'.
Each change of the text of a TextField, UTextField, TextArea or UTextArea by the user goes through the cleaner maker of the widget.

    UStrCleaner:{ mut .nextByte(b: Byte): UStr; mut .end: UStr; }
    StrCleaner:{ mut .nextByte(b: Byte): Str; mut .end: Str; }
    UStrScalarCleaner:{ mut .nextScalar(n: Nat): UStr; mut .end: UStr; }
    StrScalarCleaner:{ mut .nextScalar(n: Nat): Str; mut .end: Str; }
    UStrFixer:{ mut #(reason: BadTextReason, byteOffset: Nat, byteLength: Nat, rejectedValue: Nat): UStr; }
    StrFixer:{ mut #(reason: BadTextReason, byteOffset: Nat, byteLength: Nat, rejectedValue: Nat): Str; }
    UStrCleaners:{
      .text: imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .line: imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf8: imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf8OrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf16LeOrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf16BeOrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf32LeOrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf32BeOrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .asciiOrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .latin1OrElse(fixer: imm F[mut UStrFixer]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      .utf8Then(cleaner: imm F[mut UStrScalarCleaner]): imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner];
      }
    StrCleaners:{
      .softText: imm F[Str, mut StrCleaner];
      .softLine: imm F[Str, mut StrCleaner];
      the other methods of UStrCleaners, with Str for UStr
      }

A cleaner maker returned by a method of UStrCleaners or StrCleaners with a parameter calls that parameter once for each cleaner it makes: the result is the 'fixer' or the 'scalar cleaner' of that cleaner.

A 'run' of a cleaner maker m on an input (.size counts scalar values):

    run(m, input):
      out:= ""; start:= ""; c:= m#(start); fed:= false
      for b in input, in order: fed:= true; cut(c.nextByte(b))
      if fed && !cut(c.end) { return out }
      while start != "":
        was:= start
        if !cut(c.end) { return out }
        if start.size >= was.size { throw a deterministic exception }
      return out
    cut(r):
      if r holds no newline { out:= out + r; return false }
      out:= out + (r up to and including its first newline)
      start:= r after its first newline; c:= m#(start); fed:= false
      return true

The encoding cleaners:
A 'bad unit' is a part of the input that the encoding rejects; its BadTextReason tells why.
.utf8OrElse(fixer) decodes UTF-8; each bad unit gives the result of the fixer of the cleaner.
.utf16LeOrElse, .utf16BeOrElse, .utf32LeOrElse, .utf32BeOrElse, .asciiOrElse and .latin1OrElse do the same with their encodings.
.utf8 decodes UTF-8; a bad unit is a deterministic exception holding the BadTextReason, the byte offset and the bytes of the bad unit.
An encoding cleaner returns its starting text as it is, in front of the first character or bad unit it decodes, or at its .end.
A cleaner of the library returns the empty text while it holds a byte of an unfinished sequence.

The normalizing cleaners do their steps in order:

    'break' = carriage return newline, carriage return, newline, U+000B, U+000C, U+0085, U+2028, U+2029
    UStrCleaners.text:    decode UTF-8; bad unit -> U+FFFD; drop U+FEFF; break -> newline; NFC
    UStrCleaners.line:    UStrCleaners.text; newline -> space
    StrCleaners.softText: decode UTF-8; bad unit -> ?; drop U+FEFF; break -> newline; tab -> space; NFKD; drop what is not in Str
    StrCleaners.softLine: StrCleaners.softText; newline -> space

A normalizing cleaner normalizes its starting text followed by the text it decodes.
No cleaner of the library depends on the locale.

.utf8Then(cleaner) makes cleaners that decode UTF-8.
Each of them calls .nextScalar of its scalar cleaner with each scalar value of the starting text, then with each scalar value it decodes, with U+FFFD for a bad unit, and calls .end of its scalar cleaner at its own .end.
Each of them returns the results of its scalar cleaner, concatenated.

Reading:
A read of a file with a cleaner maker returns the result of the run of the cleaner maker on the bytes of the file.
A download with a cleaner maker returns the result of the run of the cleaner maker on the bytes of the response body.

    CapInputCursorNode:{ ...
      mut .readStr(cleaner: imm F[Str, mut StrCleaner]): Str;
      mut .readUStr(cleaner: imm F[UStr, mut UStrCleaner]): UStr;
      mut .readBytes: List[Byte];
      ...
      }

TxtFile has .readStr(cap, cleaner), .readUStr(cap, cleaner), .consumeStr(requestId, cleaner) and .consumeUStr(requestId, cleaner).
CapAssetRead has .readStr and .readUStr with a cleaner maker in the same way.

Implementation notes:
The cleaners of the library are Java classes.
A cleaner of the library and a run return a cached text for a result of size 0 or 1; for size 1, the text of Byte.size1Str or Byte.size1UStr.
